        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I think the current alphabetic sorting is just fine. However, group-items(\"git\", \"search\") are in the same sorted list as items that directly execute an action(\"Harpoon UI\") .\r\n> \r\n> In LazyVim, when pressing the leader key, items that directly execute an action are added first, sorted alphabetically. Then, the group items are added, also sorted alphabetically. For me personally, those two \"virtual\" blocks are easier to scan, as the most important keys will be on top.\r\n\r\nTo me direct alphabetic sorting adds the smallest amount of mental overhead when trying to read clue window content. As groups and non-groups have different highlighting, this seems to be the best compromise here.\r\n\r\n*But*, in order to achieve the sorting you describe (a valid one, I agree), there also needs to be information about that passed into custom sorter function. So not only `key` and `description` fields, but also `is_group` and, possibly, `has_postkeys`. This makes it more complicated, though :(",
            "created_at": "2023-08-25T10:48:48Z",
